      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nJob Description Summary The Advancement Ambassador will serve a key supportive role for the advancement areas of the division of University Advancement, Office of Engagement & Events. These areas include Advancement Services, Development, and Alumni Engagement & Events. Job Description DUTIES AND TASKS: Conduct phone calls to support donor renewal solicitation and donor stewardship plans Create and participate in video messages to support donor stewardship plans Monitor requests received through alumni engagement and sustained giving department email and phone line Conduct campus tours as needed Assist with preparation and day-of needs for meetings of the Alumni Ambassador Volunteer and College Industry Councils Assist with preparation and day-of needs for alumni, donor, and community events Support needs across the division including filing, scanning, and other office tasks REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES: Federal work-study required Must be a student enrolled at Saint Leo University ENVIRONMENT: The work environment characteristics described here are a representation of those an employee encounters while performing the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. The term “qualified individual with a disability” means an individual with a disability who, with or without reasonable accommodation, can perform the essential functions of this position. While performing the duties of this job, the employee is regularly required to communicate professionally in person, over the telephone, through email and other electronic means, move about the office and University, handle various types of media and equipment, and visually or otherwise identify, observe and assess. The employee is occasionally required to lift up to 10 pounds unless otherwise specified in the job 